    "explanation": "Both of you have been straight with each other, and the record shows the cancellation fee should not have been charged. I am refunding the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee in full to the rider, and paying the driver nothing from this fare.\n\nTo the rider: the SGD 4.00 line on the fare breakdown (cancellation_fee 4.00, total_charged 4.00) is returned to you. It is refunded because the no-show fee in this category has four conditions and at least three of them fail on the platform's own records. First, a chargeable no-show fee needs a driver 'arrived' event in the trip record (POL-NS-01 limb (a)); the trip record's arrived_at is null, so no arrival was ever logged. Second, it needs the driver's GPS trace to put him inside the pickup geofence (POL-NS-02); across 55 driver fixes the qualifying in-radius fix count is 0 against the 50 m STANDARD radius, and his closest approach to the pin was 2,240 m. Third, it needs the trip to be terminated by the driver for a recognised no-show reason (POL-NS-01 limb (d)); the record shows a rider cancellation with reason code OTHER, which is not one of the three codes the clause accepts. The waiting-period route fails too: the effective in-geofence dwell is 0 seconds against the 300-second STANDARD minimum, a 300-second shortfall (POL-NS-06), which refunds the fee whether or not the rider was present. So the fee never became chargeable.\n\nTo the driver: I accept your account. Your in-app message at 17:50:40 — 'accident, cannot come, pls cancel from your side' — and your statement that you were in a collision and asked the passenger to cancel are consistent with the telemetry, which shows you moving at 71–74 km/h throughout and never near the pickup. Nothing here treats you as someone who farmed a fee, and I am not recording a false-arrival finding against you: POL-NS-05 fires only where an 'arrived' marker was tapped and the GPS contradicts it, and no marker was tapped at all (arrived_at is null). That is also why there is no POL-NS-05(ii) referral in this ruling. You receive no compensation on this trip, but not because of anything you did wrong: POL-NS-07 pays 80 percent of the fee only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, and it is not satisfied on any limb. POL-NS-03 does not reach you either — its outer ceiling is 400 m from the pickup pin and you were more than five times that distance away, and registered_pickup_points is 1, so there is no pin-ambiguity goodwill.\n\nWhat I did with the arguments. The driver's four points are accepted: limbs (a), (b) and (d) of POL-NS-01 fail (no arrival event, no qualifying in-radius fix, reason code OTHER); POL-NS-05 is not engaged and no false-arrival referral follows; the POL-NS-07 anti-farming guard is not tripped (no_show_terminations_30d is 1, well under the 4 required, and 1 divided by completed_trips_30d of 110 is 0.009, under the 0.08 rate), so no escalation arises from profiles and no compensation is withheld on that ground; and the fare line reconciles with the schedule — the STANDARD zone-class fee is SGD 4.00 and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee is SGD 4.00, the greater of which is SGD 4.00 — so there is no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect. The rider's points are accepted on the same facts: limb (a) fails, POL-NS-02 gives a full refund on 0 qualifying fixes, POL-NS-03 cannot rescue the charge at 2,240 m, POL-NS-06 refunds on a 300-second shortfall, limb (d) fails on reason code OTHER, and POL-NS-07 pays nothing because POL-NS-01 is not satisfied. The rider's POL-NS-05 argument is right in outcome but the wrong route: no waiting clock ran, and the refund follows from POL-NS-02 and POL-NS-06 rather than from POL-NS-05(ii). The driver's contemporaneous chat message and his statement are evidence that the cancellation was driver-caused; the statement carries no weight multiplier, so it does not bear on the confidence figure.\n\nNo escalation. Every trigger under POL-NS-09 is checked and clear: the artifacts carrying the deciding facts are the trip record and the GPS trace, both COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0 and neither impaired under POL-NS-08 limbs (a)–(d) (no clock skew, 0 gap seconds, 55 fixes, chat count 1 matching the record, fare reconciling), so limb (e) does not fire; the two profiles show 0 counterparty disputes in the trailing 90 days (limb (c)) and rider no_show_disputes_30d of 0 (limb (d)); the anti-farming check does not trip (limb (d)); nothing in the artifacts contradicts anything else on arrival, dwell or rider presence (limb (b)); and my confidence of 0.95 is above the 0.70 floor (limb (a)), the deciding facts coming from artifacts at weight 1.0. The one absent artifact, the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00610-01 (MISSING, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight 0.0), is not relied on: its absence simply makes the accumulation route in POL-NS-06(i) unavailable, which is noted and changes nothing, since the dwell shortfall does not need it.\n\nOpen question for the rider's benefit, though it does not change the automated outcome: the driver says he did not know you would be charged, and the platform charged you a cancellation fee within seconds of his request. Whether the driver-side accident handling should have suppressed the fee at source is for the platform to review; it is not a money question for this ruling, and the refund above is the remedy."
